Id: mac003i
Severity: INFO
Category: kernel
Check: check_mac
References: aa-status(8); getenforce(8)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST AC-3(3); ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

A mandatory access control system is enforcing: SELinux in enforcing
mode, or AppArmor with profiles in enforce mode. The message counts
AppArmor's profiles by mode, and the detail names the ones in complain
mode, which log what they would deny and deny nothing; Ubuntu ships a
few that way. 'aa-enforce PROFILE' moves one to enforce mode once its
logged denials ('journalctl -k | grep apparmor') are understood.
"Unconfined" profiles are AppArmor's way of granting a program a
permission (such as user namespaces) without confining it. This is
informational.
